  "notes": "COMMON PATTERNS:\nGodan verb (る ending, conjugates as r-row: {見入|みい}らない, {見入|みい}ります). Takes the particle に to mark the object being gazed at: ～に{見入|みい}る.\n\nUSAGE:\nOften used with {思|おも}わず (involuntarily) to convey that the viewer was so captivated they couldn't help but stare. The nuance is always positive absorption, not hostile staring.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ～に{見入|みい}る (to gaze at ~)\n- {思|おも}わず{見入|みい}る (to involuntarily become absorbed in looking)\n- じっと{見入|みい}る (to stare fixedly)",
